---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **한국 연예인 한 사람은 몇 개 언어판에 있나.** (`/how-many-languages`)
 *
 * ⭐⭐ 사장님 지시(8/16) — 이름을 앞에. 이 지면은 **이름이 곧 결과**다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **판 수를 인기로 팔지 않는다.** 백과사전 문서가 몇 곳에 있나일 뿐이다.
 * ⛔ **평균을 안 쓴다.** 가운데가 1 인 분포라 평균은 거짓말을 한다 — 문턱으로 보인다.
 * ⛔ **명단이 깨끗하지 않다고 적는다.** 위키데이터 직업으로 골라 시인·감독이 섞였다.
 *    조용히 빼지 않고 표에 ⚠ 를 달아 이름으로 밝힌다.
 * ⛔ **0개를 「없는 사람」으로 안 센다.** 항목은 있고 문서만 없는 것이다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말은 TypeScript 다. JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다 — 붙여 쓸 곳에 {' '} 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-how-many-languages.json';

const 맨위 = d.top[0];
const 스물 = d.thresholds.find((t) => t.atLeast === 20);
const 쉰 = d.thresholds.find((t) => t.atLeast === 50);
const 하나 = d.thresholds.find((t) => t.atLeast === 1);

const TITLE = 'Psy is in 97 Wikipedias. ROSÉ of BLACKPINK is in 86, and half of Korean '
  + 'entertainers are in one';
const DESC =
  `We counted how many Wikipedia language editions hold an article about each of `
  + `${d.peopleMeasured.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean entertainers. The median is `
  + `${d.median}. Only ${쉰?.people} people reach fifty editions, and ${d.zeroEditions} have no `
  + 'article in any language.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/how-many-languages">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Of {d.peopleMeasured.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean entertainers with a Wikidata entry, the
    median one has an article in <b>{d.median}</b> language edition. The most-covered is
    {' '}<b>{맨위.name}</b> at <b>{맨위.editions}</b>. Between those two numbers is almost the whole
    story: <b>{스물?.people}</b> people ({스물?.sharePc}%) reach twenty editions and
    {' '}<b>{쉰?.people}</b> ({쉰?.sharePc}%) reach fifty.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The twenty most-covered</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Born</th><th>Language editions</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.top.map((x) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{x.name}{x.notAnEntertainer && <span class="warnmark"> ⚠</span>}</td>
              <td class="fine">{x.born}</td>
              <td><b>{x.editions}</b></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="warn">⚠ {d.panelIsNotClean}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where everyone else sits</h2>
    <p class="note">{d.thresholdsAreOurs}</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>At least</th><th>People</th><th>Share of panel</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.thresholds.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{t.atLeast} {t.atLeast === 1 ? 'edition' : 'editions'}</td>
              <td>{t.people.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td class="fine">{t.sharePc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      <b>{d.zeroEditions}</b> people have <b>zero</b>. {d.zeroMeans} They stay in the denominator
      for that reason — dropping them would turn {d.peopleMeasured.toLocaleString('en-US')} into
      {' '}{하나?.people.toLocaleString('en-US')} and quietly raise every share on this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The obvious objection, tested</h2>
    <p>
      Psy's song is from 2012. Editors have had fourteen years to write him up, and Jennie's
      Wikidata item has had rather fewer. If coverage were mostly a function of time, the oldest
      people in the panel would be the widest.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Born</th><th>People</th><th>Median editions</th>
          <th>Reaching 20 editions</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.byDecade.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{r.decade}</td>
              <td class="fine">{r.people.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{r.median}</td>
              <td><b>{r.atLeastWidePc}%</b></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {d.timeObjection?.ruledOut && (
      <p>
        <strong>They are the narrowest.</strong> {d.timeObjection.reading} The widest cohort is the
        one born in the 1990s at {d.timeObjection.newerCohortsWidestPc}%, against
        {' '}{d.timeObjection.olderCohortsWidestPc}% for the widest cohort born before 1970. Psy is
        an outlier inside a thinner generation, not a beneficiary of one.
      </p>
    )}
    <p class="note">
      We ran this control because we had just been caught by the same mechanism going the other way:
      a 69% fall in new Korean groups that turned out to be
      {' '}<a href="/article/the-69-per-cent-fall-we-did-not-publish">how fast the source records
      them</a>, not how many there were.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note"><b>Limits</b> — {d.limitation}</p>
    <p class="note"><b>Source</b> — {d.source}, {d.window}.</p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/how-many-languages" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warnmark { color: #b45309; }
</style>
